paragraphs.text:
In allowing the application, the

High Court has relied upon on the following circumstances:
(i) The appellant was in custody for a period of two and a half years;
(ii) Out of seventy-six witnesses only twenty-five have been examined;
(iii) There was a delay in lodging the FIR;
(iv) While the initial FSL report did not contain any reference to the use of the

 Ketamine, it was after four months that police had developed a case that

 Ketamine was administered to the deceased; and
(v) The co-accused had been enlarged on bail.
